                <pb facs="0731" n="633" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg633"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Lord
                            Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1925.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note, No. 270, of the 17th instant, conveying to the Government
                    of the United States an expression of the heartfelt sympathy of the governor and
                    people of the Windward Islands on account of the disaster at Galveston.</p>
                <p>I beg that you will assure Sir A. Moloney that his sympathetic mesage is
                    sincerely appreciated by the Government of the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
